    {
      "version": "1.4",
      "releaseNotes": "- Bugs fixed.\n- Aesthetic improvements.\n- iPad support.",
      "seenAt": "2019-10-23T08:18:50Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "2.0",
      "releaseNotes": "- New circuits\n- Possibility of turning left and right\n- New cars\n\n* The original classification of the game has been saved, available for consultation, to always remember the beginnings of the game.",
      "seenAt": "2020-01-24T15:22:03Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "2.0.1",
      "releaseNotes": "- After the last big update, we have solved a bug in speed management.",
      "seenAt": "2020-01-24T18:37:56Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "2.0.2",
      "releaseNotes": "- New screenshots to explain better the game\n- Aesthetic improvements\n- Solved bug with some circuits could not be opened on the Apple Watch",
      "seenAt": "2020-01-27T19:16:39Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "2.0.3",
      "releaseNotes": "- Fixed bugs of some circuits in the app for Apple Watch. The quality and size of the images has been reduced.",
      "seenAt": "2020-02-11T13:17:00Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "2.1.0",
      "releaseNotes": "- We have improved the circuit loader on the Apple Watch. Some Apple Watch may still have an error due to lack of memory when loading the circuit. We have reduced the images to the maximum, but for the moment we still have no solution to the problem, but we will be alert to possible updates of WatchOS to solve the problem once and for all. THANKS for understanding and support received.\n- A new circuit has been added",
      "seenAt": "2020-02-15T21:18:33Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "2.2.0",
      "releaseNotes": "- Fixed bug in scenario 3\n- Added sound",
      "seenAt": "2020-03-31T02:06:02Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "2.2.1",
      "releaseNotes": "- Left / Right circuits load more efficiently. Crashes on Apple Watch should be reduced.\n- Left / Right circuits for Apple Watch are really hard. Difficulty has been reduced, now there are collisions.",
      "seenAt": "2020-05-18T02:55:18Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "2.2.2",
      "releaseNotes": "We continue trying to improve the efficiency of the circuits for Apple Watch. With this update, we reduce memory errors on Circuits 1 and 2. Verified with an Apple Watch Series 3. You can see a video on our social networks playing in a series 3.",
      "seenAt": "2020-06-08T21:09:19Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "2.2.3",
      "releaseNotes": "- Fixed bugs circuit 3 for Apple Watch. The circuitry on the Apple Watch has been trimmed to make it lighter.\n- Non-clickable advertising has been added to the circuits to give a more racing appearance.\n- Updated SDK 14",
      "seenAt": "2020-09-21T23:11:51Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "2.3",
      "releaseNotes": "- New circuit 4\n- Small aesthetic improvements",
      "seenAt": "2020-10-02T13:47:49Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "2.4",
      "releaseNotes": "- New circuit 5\n- Aesthetic improvements",
      "seenAt": "2020-12-04T01:14:35Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "2.5.0",
      "releaseNotes": "- New circuit 6\n- Aesthetic improvements\n- Ability to remove advertising through IAP",
      "seenAt": "2021-02-19T15:14:29Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "2.5.1",
      "releaseNotes": "- Requested user authorization for \"App Tracking Transparency\"\n- Added support for Apple Watch 7",
